From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: extra brightness: the guest's SDR frames up to 2x on an XDR display

What: with the app's switch extraBrightness (its own defaults key, read
live: QEMU runs as the app; KVO also reports a change from another
process, and the key is read again when the window is seen again or the
app becomes active; OMACVM_EXTRA_BRIGHT=1 for a QEMU not started as the
app), the IOSurface present draws the guest's SDR frames through a shader
(ui/omacvm-bright.h) into half-float surfaces tagged extended linear
sRGB: decoded from sRGB to linear light and multiplied by g, and the
layer shows them with EDR and toneMapMode never. g = the window's
display's EDR headroom now, at most 2, in hundredths, read every 250 ms
on the main thread while the switch is on, the window is seen and its
display's EDR potential is above 2.05; a move of 0.02 or more, the switch
turning on or off, or a new display redraws the newest frame at once
(omacvm_bright_bh, in both present modes, also on a static desktop). The
surfaces carry kIOSurfaceContentHeadroom 2.0, so macOS raises the panel's
headroom only as far as the frames need.

It goes back by itself: off, the next frame takes the plain 8-bit path
and the layer drops EDR; out of sight no frame is drawn
(omacvm-cocoa-present-unseen.patch) and the look stops; on another
display without the headroom g is 1 and the frames are 8-bit. The
surfaces actually there decide how a frame is drawn, not the switch, so a
frame drawn into the other kind during the half-second realloc hold-off
keeps its own colours (the boot logo too: its clear colour is decoded,
and it stays at 1x). PQ frames (HDR, ADR 0049) are never boosted: "not
with HDR yet".

Why: the user asked for an opt-in extra brightness for the VM's window
(bright light). The guest cannot do it: Hyprland gives PQ windows a fixed
reference white whatever sdr_max_luminance says, and SDR guests have no
EDR; a plain 2x of a PQ frame would double and clip its highlights.
macOS's own tone mapping halves SDR white below full headroom (ADR 0049),
hence never.

Fallbacks: no IOSurface present (GPU safe mode, OMACVM_GL_PRESENT=layer),
untagged colour (OMACVM_GL_COLOR=native), half-float surfaces failing
(present_deep_failed) or the shader not compiling: off for the run, said
once. The shader is made on present_ctx the first time it is needed,
never at start: a failure there cannot stop a VM.

Logs (qemu.log, once per change): "cocoa: extra brightness: on, 2.00x",
"held back by macOS, 1.40x" (after 2 s below 1.90x), "not on this display
(EDR potential 2.00)", "not with HDR yet", "off (switch off)", "off
(why)". OMACVM_TEST_EDR="potential,headroom" stands in for the window's
display (the app passes it to test builds only).

Threads: the main thread reads the switch and NSScreen and writes
omacvm_bright_wanted and omacvm_bright_gain_c (qatomic); QEMU's thread
reads them when it draws; the commit thread gets each frame's kind with
the frame (PresentFrame.linear) for the layer's EDR.

Cost while on: 8 bytes a pixel instead of 4 for the present surfaces
(5 with vsync: about +154 MB at 3456x2234) and one pow() per pixel.

Upstream: OmacVM only (IOSurface present, the app's settings).
Test: app/runtime/Tests/display/test-extra-brightness.sh (rules, wiring;
the checks catch code without it); on screen: work notes
tracks/night-brightness.md (headroom with the switch on and off, hidden,
VM stopped, on the M1 Max XDR panel).

